nch","Italian","German","Spanish - Spain","Portuguese - Brazil","Portuguese - Portugal","Simplified Chinese","Spanish - Latin America","Traditional Chinese","Japanese","Korean"],"min":[["OS","Windows XP or better"],["Processor","Intel CPU 2.3 Ghz or better"],["Memory","8 GB RAM"],["Graphics","Intel HD Graphics 4000 or better (2GB or more of VRAM)"],["DirectX","Version 10"],["Storage","4 GB available space"]],"rec":[],"deck":3,"blurb":"Minesweeper-style tile flipping drives this roguelite puzzle game set in the land of Beebom. The player hunts a tyrannical King across procedurally generated maze maps, turning over tiles and working out where the King's henchmen are hiding. Those henchmen can be dodged or fought in turn-based encounters, and over a hundred items and abilities gathered along the way change the approach before a final showdown in Beebom City.\n\nHand-animated art from the animation studio BUCK and an original score by Antfood give Let's! Revolution! a distinctive look and sound. It is single-player with full controller support, and it suits puzzle fans who enjoy deduction, especially those drawn to replayable roguelite runs."}}